From 723afd756caab2e97b4ecaa2c622279acab9d9d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Rademakers <sven@turingpi.com>
Date: Sat, 05 Jul 2026 17:35:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] net: dsa: rtl8365mb: add hardware LAG / trunk offload

Add DSA port_lag_join/leave/change hooks and program the RTL8367-class
trunk tables so two user ports can hash in hardware when enslaved to a
Linux bond.

Origin / credits:
  rtl8365mb DSA baseline: Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>
  Bridge / VLAN / FDB offload this builds on: Luiz Angelo Daros de Luca's
    realtek_forward series (local backport in net-dsa/0001).
  PORT_TRUNK_* register map / dumb-mode semantics: Realtek rtl8367c
    vendor SDK (RTL8370MB-CG validated on Turing Pi 2).

Also:
- set ds->num_lag_ids so DSA assigns lag->id (required for port_lag_join)
- allow single-member join in lag_can_offload (program HW at 2 members)
- limit trunk groups to 0-1 (only these have hash map registers)
- enable trunk dumb mode (CPU LACP + ASIC data plane)
- trap LACP RMA 01:80:c2:00:00:02 to CPU (RMA_CTRL02); HW trunk
  otherwise swallows partner LACPDUs so bonding never sees RX

Replace unused HSR ops with LAG ops (CONFIG_HSR is off in this tree,
so dsa_port_simple_hsr_* are not declared).

Signed-off-by: Sven Rademakers <sven@turingpi.com>
